# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.coverage*
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Throwaway working area. Scratch scripts, probes, and any environment that has
# to be built for a one-off task live here and nowhere else.
#
# This exists because they previously lived in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp, where a
# one-off task installed a ~1 GB PyTorch environment to generate the encoder
# parity reference. A gigabyte of unsigned native DLLs appearing at once under
# a user-profile temp path is the shape antivirus heuristics look for, and
# Avast blocked it — correctly, on the evidence available to it. Nothing was
# corrupted, but the location was the problem: work that belongs to this
# project should be visible inside this project, not buried in a temp folder
# the developer never looks at.
.tmp/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
next-env.d.ts

# Agent tooling — kept local. The workflow that produced this repository is not
# part of what it delivers, so the skills, subagent definitions, and the
# agent-context files stay untracked.
/.claude/
.claudeignore
/.github/agents/
/.github/instructions/
/.github/skills/
/.github/sddp-config.md
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md

# `specs/` and `project-instructions.md` are deliberately tracked. The
# specification, plan, ADRs, checklists, and analysis report record why this
# scaffold is shaped the way it is — which is most of what makes the repository
# worth reading. Do not re-add them here.

# Local backup of pre-rewrite git history (created during history scrub)
/.git.backup-pre-scrub/

# Compose reads this automatically and it holds machine-specific host-port
# overrides (PRC_DB_PORT and friends). Several checkouts of this repository can
# share one machine, so the right value differs per working copy and must never
# be committed.
/.env

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

/gitignored/
